    "body": "Thanks for your interest in our work. You can download the CamylaNetBench dataset here: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/11BrGWWZw8yr2o2AkVV9o5e7de-T9nngz?usp=sharing. We recommend using either CamylaNet (https://github.com/yifangao112/CamylaNet) or nnU-Net (https://github.com/mic-dkfz/nnunet) for preprocessing. After that, you can access the dataset splits in splits_final.json.\n\nWe use Fold 0 for training and testing by default. The splits are fixed in these frameworks, so you don't need to perform any extra partitioning. We need some time to organize the results for each baseline, but you can go ahead and run CamylaNet in the meantime.",
